Subject: [PATCH 11140/11171] [outer-loop] Quiet hour: the standing cascade is
 spent, not stuck

exp6999 reads complete_disqualified_blinded_feature_shortcut_gate with its
gated score at 0, which is terminal, so that cascade line will show
permanently. exp7000 correctly reads blocked_gate_check_failed. Nothing is
wedged; the dashboard reports a resolved condition, the same property already
recorded for the attention line.

Base rate checked and it refutes the tempting claim: of six recent
cascade-blocking upstreams, two are terminal and four are blocked_*, so
'the cascade line usually shows spent cascades' is not supported. Only the two
the dashboard happened to display this session were terminal, which is an
anecdote.

Recorded as a thing to watch rather than a finding: both disqualifications are
shortcut gates firing, on two consecutive milestones, both on feature banks.
That is the gate working. Whether the planner keeps proposing a shortcut-prone
design is a question two data points cannot answer.

